<!-- The E.D. Cal. complaint's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of the
     typst template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 12 pt (size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes
     (typst pitch, L.R. 130(c) double spaced) with a half-inch indent; counsel, caption and signature lines in 12 pt
     boxes (typst pitch-single: half a numbered line, as filed). Pleading paper as typst/caed-complaint.typ: letter, top and bottom margins 1 in (27
     numbered lines of 24 pt between them), left 1.5 in, right 1 in; the numbers 1 to 27 in the left margin as one
     frame of exact 24 pt lines anchored to the page at the top margin, ending an inch from the page edge (header
     rIdCaedLines, L.R. 130(b)); a double rule at the text's left edge and a single rule at its right (page borders);
     the footer (L.R. 130(d)): the document's description (the SUBJECT property, which docx/caed-complaint.lua sets
     from footer_title) and the page number on one 10 pt line in a 12 pt box, its foot 54 pt above the page edge (1080
     twips: where typst sets it, 6 pt below the last numbered line). Twips: 20 x pt. -->
